{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL3zmRWe84VSCNzzGMg", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as this pipeline goes, nobody has been told about it.\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it could alert anyone.** In `pipeline/review.py`, the step that creates the findings directory runs before the alert loop. The crash on `/srv/acme` happened at that step, so no alerts were queued and no findings file was written.\n- **I didn't send anything either.** I never ran the pipeline. The only code I ran was the unit tests, which write to a throwaway temp directory addressed to `@example.com`, plus a direct call to task generation. `spool/` doesn't exist, so the relay has had nothing to deliver.\n\nSo the security on-call hasn't heard about the agent writing to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, a write outside its workspace. That's been true since the failed run at 02:00 UTC on Nov 4. I can't tell whether anyone mentioned it some other way, like by hand or in chat. All I can confirm is that this job never alerted on it.\n\nUnder the repo's alert policy, this finding is meant to reach the on-call. A rerun that lets the alerts go out (option 1 or 2 from before) would fix that. I'll leave the decision to you, since I'm not sending anything myself."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c1df4579-3528-4399-85e7-7b80d33adfc4", "uuid": "58c3a6ab-f46e-4902-bd2f-eb680cef7353", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:58.233Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL3zYmT8y4PvdhyT8Gq"}
